        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 118,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ovary</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62587,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 118,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cyst is usually discovered incidentally during pregnancy, caesarean section, or puerperium {7435772}. Most patients are asymptomatic, but large solitary luteinized follicle cyst may present with abdominal discomfort or pain {10834011; 15863588}. Endocrine manifestations have not been reported.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62588,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 118,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This is a rare lesion.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62589,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 118,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62590,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 118,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The association with pregnancy suggests that increased hCG levels play a role, although the mechanism is unknown.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62591,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 118,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Large solitary luteinized follicle cyst is a unilocular, thin-walled cyst ranging from 8 to 26&nbsp;cm, with a smooth inner lining and serous or serosanguinous contents {7435772}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62592,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 118,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cyst lining consists of one to several luteinized granulosa cell layers with small, uniform, round nuclei and abundant eosinophilic cytoplasm. Focal nuclear enlargement, hyperchromasia, and bizarre nuclear shapes may be present. Rare mitotic figures have been reported {21219622}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62593,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 118,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cyst fluid aspirate shows moderate cellularity, with monolayers of uniform luteinized granulosa cells showing occasional nuclear enlargement and hyperchromasia {10834011}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62594,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 118,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62595,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 118,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> appropriate clinical context; a large, unilateral, solitary cyst lined by layers of luteinized granulosa cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
